course: dictionary
lesson: 11743
title: Backlighting: light from behind
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Backlighting is light that is placed behind something. Look at the parts of the word: back means behind, and lighting means light. «The screen backlighting made the words easy to read in the dark.» The light sits behind the screen, so the screen glows and the words stand out.
explain: Backlighting also works for keyboards. «Turn on the keyboard backlighting so you can see the keys in the dark.» The light comes from behind or under the keys, so each key is lit up and easy to see.
explain: In photos, backlighting means the light comes from behind the person or thing. «The photographer used backlighting, so the girl's outline glowed against the bright sky.» Her edges shine, which can make a photo look dramatic.
fact: Backlighting is a noun: it is the name of the light placed behind something.
fact: «Backlighting» means light placed behind something, such as a screen, a keyboard or a person in a photo.
fact: In a photo, backlighting makes the edges of a person or thing glow.
fact: «Screen backlighting» and «keyboard backlighting» are phrases you may see on a laptop, tablet or phone.
fact: Back means behind and lighting means light, so backlighting means light from behind.
exercise: «Turn on the keyboard backlighting so you can see the keys in the dark.» What is keyboard backlighting? | *Light behind the keys so they can be seen | A loud sound made when you type | A keyboard made of wood | A soft cloth for cleaning the keys
exercise: «The photographer used backlighting, so the girl's outline glowed against the bright sky.» What does backlighting do in this photo? | It makes the sky disappear | It turns the photo into a painting | *It makes the edges of the girl glow | It makes the girl start to sing
exercise: What does the word «backlighting» mean? | A dark shadow placed in front of something | A type of paint for walls | *Light placed behind something | A loud noise made by a machine
test: «The screen backlighting made the words easy to read in the dark.» Where is the light in this sentence? | *Behind the screen | Inside the printer | Far away in the sky | Under the desk
test: In a photo, what does backlighting make happen? | The subject disappears completely | The camera stops working | The photo turns black and white | *The edges of the subject look bright and glowing
exam: Ella says, «The backlighting on my phone is too bright.» What is the backlighting? | *The light behind the phone screen | The sound the phone makes | The battery inside the phone | The phone's case
